ROOT-CAUSE ANALYSIS — every gate failure is PRE-EXISTING and OUT-OF-SCOPE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The repo is in the documented "parallel surface" WIP state. The whole-app
`xcodebuild ... build test` target cannot link/compile yet for reasons that exist
independently of this surface and live in files this prompt is NOT allowed to edit
(Allowed files: TripSummaryWidget.*, the log file):

  A. *.Tests.swift colocated in the app-target source path import XCTest, but XCTest
     only links into XCTest bundles — so the app target fails dependency resolution
     on the FIRST such file (DigitalTwinWidget.Tests.swift, alphabetically before
     TripSummary). This is systemic: EVERY widget (incl. MileageStats, LocationFavorites,
     and this one) colocates a *.Tests.swift per the house convention; project.yml routes
     only Tests/Unit to the test bundle. Fixing it requires editing project.yml — out of scope.

  B. Duplicate definitions of the shared grid primitives across sibling surfaces
     (a redeclaration conflict once the module reaches type-check):
